## 6. Stable Content Identity

Every knowledge record must have a globally unique and stable internal content ID.

Distinguish between:

- Internal content ID.
- URL slug.
- Official source identifier.
- Official decision ID.
- Official requirement ID.
- Source document path.
- Content version.
- Display title.

Do not use the title or file path as the permanent identity.

Do not invent official D-* or R-* identifiers.

Identifiers introduced by Knowledge Hub must be clearly distinguishable from official Teranoo ERP identifiers.

For example:

- `D-PLAT-01` is an official ERP decision ID.
- `R-IDN-3` is an official ERP requirement ID.
- `IR-050` is an independent review note ID.
- `FAC-018` is an official future consideration ID.
- An internal Knowledge Hub document ID identifies a platform content record.

Renaming a document or changing its title must not break existing content relationships.

