## 9. Markdown and Frontmatter Support

Implement safe server-side loading of local Markdown documents.

Use mature, maintained libraries where appropriate, such as:

- gray-matter.
- remark.
- remark-gfm.
- rehype.
- rehype-sanitize.
- Zod or an equivalent runtime schema validation library.

Select the smallest compatible dependency set required by the implementation.

Document all additions.

### Markdown rendering requirements

Support:

- Headings.
- Paragraphs.
- Ordered and unordered lists.
- Tables.
- Blockquotes.
- Code blocks.
- Inline code.
- Links.
- Images.
- Footnotes where supported by the selected renderer.
- Horizontal dividers.
- Mixed Arabic and English content.

### Security requirements

- Do not execute arbitrary JavaScript from content.
- Do not enable unrestricted MDX execution.
- Do not trust raw HTML by default.
- Sanitize rendered content using an explicit safe policy.
- Validate link and image protocols.
- Prevent filesystem path traversal.
- Do not expose arbitrary local files through document routes.
- Do not expose unpublished content through public APIs or client bundles.
- Restrict document loading to approved content collections.

MDX may be evaluated later if controlled interactive embedding is required.

Do not introduce unrestricted executable content in TASK-002.

