## 14. Source and Publication Governance

The Knowledge Hub is an authorized public knowledge-sharing platform.

However, public application visibility does not grant automatic permission to publish every file from a private source repository.

Implement an explicit publishing boundary.

Content must not become publicly available merely because a file exists in a local source directory.

Only explicitly publication-authorized records may enter the public content registry and public search index.

### Required behavior

- Draft and unpublished records must not be included in public output.
- Publication authorization must be separate from official ERP approval.
- An approved ERP document is not automatically authorized for public redistribution.
- Source attribution must remain available.
- Existing copyright notices must be preserved.
- Secrets, credentials, customer data, and sensitive operational information must never be published.
- Do not create a license for the original ERP project.
- Do not infer third-party redistribution rights from public website availability.

### External research sources

The platform may eventually publish original project-authored research reports and properly attributed source references.

Do not copy entire copyrighted third-party documentation pages into the website without appropriate authorization.

Do not connect to GitHub APIs or retrieve private repository contents in this task.

